# Global Token & Efficiency Constraints

## 1. Context Minimization
- NEVER read entire folders or repositories unless explicitly ordered.
- Request explicit permission via `@` file targets before analyzing code outside the immediate scope.
- If a task can be done by looking at a single file, only read that file.

## 2. Model Tiering
- Default to using the fastest, lowest-token model (e.g., Gemini Flash) for boilerplate, explanations, and minor edits.
- Flag the user to switch to a higher-tier model (e.g., Pro) ONLY for complex debugging or structural refactoring.

## 3. Session State Maintenance
- Maintain a running, ultra-compact `working.md` file in the root to track current progress.
- Read this `working.md` at the start of each task to prevent re-analyzing past chat history or re-scanning the repo.
- Maintain a separate `phases_summary.md` file that tracks all implementation phases. Summarize the important implementations in that phase in simple terms with a clear flow. Always append information as we go along, and only update existing information if the logic was actually modified for that particular phase.
